        "abstract": "Radio transmission measurements have been made at 3675 megacycles on the 130-mile path between Miami and Key West, Florida, which is largely over watery wastes of the Everglades and shallow sea waters of the Florida Keys. Path loss and fading characteristics for this terrain were not found to m e r materially from the characteristics of hilly or mountainous paths in the northeastern section of the country.",
